WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.034
A student wants a database for autism

00:00:03.054 --> 00:00:05.611
research. A catalogue search returns

00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:08.034
nothing. Should the system conclude that

00:00:08.054 --> 00:00:11.024
the library has nothing useful, or treat

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.789
the failure as information for another

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:14.864
attempt? Pause and consider what a

00:00:14.884 --> 00:00:17.415
database record is likely to say.

00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:21.691
The chapter’s loop broadens to related

00:00:21.711 --> 00:00:24.462
subject areas and recovers useful database

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:27.194
names. The request was for a database

00:00:27.214 --> 00:00:29.694
about a subject, not necessarily a

00:00:29.714 --> 00:00:32.167
database named after that subject.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.312
Recovery changes how the search is used.

00:00:36.227 --> 00:00:38.038
The author’s June twenty twenty six

00:00:38.058 --> 00:00:40.951
demonstration replayed selected database

00:00:40.971 --> 00:00:42.987
queries from twenty twenty three zero

00:00:43.007 --> 00:00:45.577
result logs against the library’s Primo

00:00:45.597 --> 00:00:49.507
index, through a model and an MCP server.

00:00:49.669 --> 00:00:52.175
The request asked for a database for each

00:00:52.195 --> 00:00:52.948
topic.

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:55.172
The examples were selected rather than

00:00:55.192 --> 00:00:58.174
sampled, and newer models answered older

00:00:58.194 --> 00:01:01.319
queries. Read the account as exploratory

00:01:01.339 --> 00:01:04.437
failure recovery, not a success rate, a

00:01:04.457 --> 00:01:07.015
controlled benchmark, or a comparison

00:01:07.035 --> 00:01:09.785
proving superiority over human searchers.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.513
The comparison used Primo’s single pass

00:01:13.533 --> 00:01:15.510
Natural Language Search over the same

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:19.222
index. For autism it produced a plausible

00:01:19.242 --> 00:01:22.172
OR expression including autistic disorder,

00:01:22.438 --> 00:01:25.601
ASD, autism spectrum, neurodevelopmental

00:01:25.621 --> 00:01:27.714
disorder and pervasive developmental

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:30.999
disorder. It still returned zero results.

00:01:31.565 --> 00:01:33.534
The source’s six terms stayed at the

00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:34.874
autism concept.

00:01:35.036 --> 00:01:37.413
The single pass rewrite did not use the

00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:40.209
zero result response to revise the query.

00:01:40.371 --> 00:01:42.954
More synonyms were not the same operation

00:01:42.974 --> 00:01:45.170
as choosing a broader subject area.

00:01:46.076 --> 00:01:49.205
The loop broadened autism into psychology,

00:01:49.225 --> 00:01:52.001
medicine, education and disability.

00:01:52.164 --> 00:01:53.832
In the selected example it returned

00:01:53.852 --> 00:01:58.084
PsycINFO, Education Research Complete and

00:01:58.182 --> 00:02:00.726
SocINDEX. Those names are reported

00:02:00.746 --> 00:02:03.110
outcomes from the chapter, not searches

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.733
conducted for this video.

00:02:05.303 --> 00:02:08.262
The keyword oriented endpoint did not need

00:02:08.282 --> 00:02:10.891
a new scoring formula for that sequence to

00:02:10.911 --> 00:02:13.430
become useful. The controller reformulated

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.530
the request and tried again.

00:02:16.451 --> 00:02:18.891
Other selected examples turned cost of

00:02:18.911 --> 00:02:21.197
living into inflation, household

00:02:21.217 --> 00:02:23.736
expenditure and consumer prices.

00:02:23.872 --> 00:02:26.082
Rolex watches became a question about

00:02:26.102 --> 00:02:28.904
luxury goods, producing Statista and

00:02:28.924 --> 00:02:31.906
Passport. The typo statis resolved to

00:02:31.926 --> 00:02:32.949
Statista.

00:02:33.533 --> 00:02:37.260
The refinituv example reached LSEG, but

00:02:37.281 --> 00:02:39.670
that illustrates the dating problem: the

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.235
recovered rebrand postdated the original

00:02:42.255 --> 00:02:45.302
query. A newer model knows things an older

00:02:45.322 --> 00:02:46.448
model might not.

00:02:46.598 --> 00:02:49.052
Do not attribute every improvement to the

00:02:49.072 --> 00:02:50.108
loop alone.

00:02:51.031 --> 00:02:53.702
The chapter reports that a holdings CSV

00:02:53.722 --> 00:02:56.563
also worked for the selected examples, and

00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:58.560
a smaller model made little difference

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.060
there. That does not establish that model

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.998
capability is generally irrelevant, or

00:03:04.018 --> 00:03:06.665
that MCP itself caused recovery.

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:10.196
The examples support feedback, broadening

00:03:10.216 --> 00:03:12.335
and another attempt, while changing other

00:03:12.355 --> 00:03:13.804
parts of the setup too.

00:03:13.979 --> 00:03:16.511
They do not isolate the loop as the sole

00:03:16.531 --> 00:03:19.810
cause. Fixed or adaptive workflows could

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.890
also implement useful retries; better

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.989
retrieval still matters.

00:03:25.885 --> 00:03:27.588
The model can draw on public knowledge

00:03:27.608 --> 00:03:30.062
about familiar databases and subject

00:03:30.082 --> 00:03:33.168
areas. A little known or newly licensed

00:03:33.188 --> 00:03:35.655
database may receive less help.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:38.696
Current coverage, field quirks, embargo

00:03:38.716 --> 00:03:41.274
dates and this institution’s actual

00:03:41.294 --> 00:03:43.645
entitlements are local facts it cannot

00:03:43.665 --> 00:03:44.997
safely infer.

00:03:45.553 --> 00:03:47.971
Those facts need authoritative library

00:03:47.991 --> 00:03:50.767
information. Recovery does not remove that

00:03:50.787 --> 00:03:53.215
work; it changes where it belongs.

00:03:53.377 --> 00:03:55.394
A specialised request about particular

00:03:55.414 --> 00:03:57.971
variables, companies and years can still

00:03:57.991 --> 00:04:00.805
exceed the available knowledge or tools.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.099
A zero result can become an observation

00:04:04.119 --> 00:04:06.457
that informs the next action, while the

00:04:06.477 --> 00:04:08.571
retriever’s scoring function stays

00:04:08.591 --> 00:04:11.534
unchanged. In these selected examples,

00:04:11.554 --> 00:04:13.750
that helped recover useful results.

00:04:13.926 --> 00:04:17.101
It does not show that every retry succeeds

00:04:17.121 --> 00:04:19.304
or requires agentic control.

00:04:19.851 --> 00:04:22.585
Record the failed query, the new action,

00:04:22.851 --> 00:04:25.305
what came back and why the search stopped.

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:28.037
Choose control for the actual task and

00:04:28.057 --> 00:04:30.395
supply current local knowledge.

00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:33.385
The completed pipeline now lets us ask a

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:35.382
diagnostic question: where did a

00:04:35.402 --> 00:04:37.057
particular search go wrong?
